15. How this fits with your existing product-building work
You have also been exploring Stratus, an intelligent cloud-drive and data-management product. 

There is a potential longer-term relationship between these ideas, but I would keep the products and security boundaries separate initially:
- Stratus: Cloud-file access, synchronization, and document management.
- Vaultora: Passwords, credentials, encryption keys, and sensitive records.
- Possible future integration: A user-controlled way to access a credential or authorized secret related to a file or service, without exposing vault contents to the file-management system.
Do not combine all of the infrastructure into one large application before either product has a clear threat model. A credential vault has different security requirements from a general-purpose cloud drive, and a compromise of one should not automatically compromise the other.
16. Final recommendation
I would pursue this business only with a focused product strategy:
The launch strategy I would choose
1. Start with freelancers and small digital agencies. They have a clear need to manage multiple client credentials.
2. Build a secure password vault first. Password generation, encrypted notes, reliable synchronization, and browser autofill are the foundation.
3. Differentiate through client workspaces. Make organizing and sharing credentials for multiple clients exceptionally simple.
4. Introduce paid team features. Add permissions, controlled sharing, audit events, and access revocation.
5. Expand into the broader digital vault. Add structured sensitive records, encrypted files, family access, and carefully designed AI-assisted organization.
6. Make security a product requirement. Independently assess the implementation before trusting it with real customer credentials at scale.

The strongest business proposition is not “another LastPass.” It is a secure, easy-to-use vault for people and small teams who manage many digital accounts, credentials, and sensitive records.

One final decision will materially affect the architecture, budget, and launch plan: whether you want to build a consumer-focused vault, a business-focused vault, or a hybrid product from the beginning. My recommendation is a hybrid architecture with a freelancer-and-agency-first launch, so the first paying customers can fund expansion into family and individual plans.